{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 15: what people believe. Demand grows steadily from week 10. The manager sees it late, and, extrapolating the trend, may overshoot. }
Demand=
	100 + RAMP(2, 10, 40)
	~	units/week
	~	What customers really buy: flat at 100, then growing by 2 each week from week 10 to week 40.
	|
Perceived demand=
	EXPECT(Demand, 6)
	~	units/week
	~	What the manager believes demand is: the fact, noticed with a lag of about 6 weeks.
	|
Perceived trend=
	EXPECT(Demand, 6, measure=trend)
	~	1/week
	~	The growth the manager thinks they see, as a fraction of demand per week.
	|
Expected demand in 8 weeks=
	EXPECT(Demand, 6, ahead=8)
	~	units/week
	~	Where the manager expects demand to be in 8 weeks, extrapolating the trend.
	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ week ~ |
FINAL TIME = 60 ~ week ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.25 ~ week ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.25 ~ week ~ |
